# What not to upload when deploying.
#
# Vercel only falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent, and that
# fallback is not dependable: across these three projects it excluded env files
# here and in 4i Productions, shipped invoICE's `.env`, and shipped 4i
# Productions' SQLite database. All four files were gitignored.
#
# Nothing here leaked — this is to keep it that way. Because .vercelignore
# replaces the fallback outright, the ordinary exclusions are repeated too.
#
# Note what must NOT be excluded: `content/` holds the gated PDFs, read off disk
# by /api/download/[slug]. They live outside public/ on purpose so they can only
# be served behind a signed token, and leaving them out would break every
# download link.

# Secrets. These belong in Vercel's project settings, nowhere else.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.admin-password.txt

# Dependencies and build output — Vercel installs and builds its own.
node_modules
.next
out
build

# Local state and tooling
.git
.vercel
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
